ue] [17592186672584 1068 #edb/ref 17592186672637 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672584 1068 #edb/ref 17592186672640 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672584 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672584 1071 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-6xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672584 1072 #uuid "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672584 1074 "First, we define $f(x,y)=-6xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive”; “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative”." 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672585 1080 "false" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672585 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672585 1083 #uuid "1862e18d-986b-5d28-b0d2-296a0d3c1090" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672590 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672586 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672631 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672586 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672586 1077 "At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672586 1078 #edb/ref 17592186672590 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672586 1079 #uuid "1ca97b16-ffef-5260-ac53-9f232f048a0b" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672587 1080 "false" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672587 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672587 1083 #uuid "1de02087-3c61-50b7-b52b-577a820446ec" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672588 1080 "true" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672588 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672588 1083 #uuid "233c0192-884a-5254-95fa-e1c83b7f8fb4" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672589 1080 "false" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672589 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672589 1083 #uuid "23d36483-289a-586a-a99a-5ab37d982a59" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672590 1080 "false" 13194139538697 17592186045443 t