611 1077 "At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672611 1078 #edb/ref 17592186672644 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672611 1079 #uuid "71ebc04d-0aa8-567a-8462-97edb6e92033" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672612 1068 #edb/ref 17592186672595 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672612 1068 #edb/ref 17592186672606 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672612 1068 #edb/ref 17592186672619 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672612 1068 #edb/ref 17592186672626 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672612 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672612 1071 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672612 1072 #uuid "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672612 1074 "First, we define $f(x,y)=-2xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” only." 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672613 1080 "true" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672613 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672613 1083 #uuid "7800afa6-b30d-59d9-ac68-f065e4153673" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672614 1080 "true" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672614 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672614 1083 #uuid "780a48db-d701-578f-b2d1-13c5af2d0077" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672615 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672583 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672615 1075 #edb/ref 17592186672620 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672615 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672615 1077 "At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672615 1078 #edb/ref 17592186672583 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672615 1079 #uuid "79aad520-644b-54cf-9059-eada322e4888" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672616 1080 "true" 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672616 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538697 17592186045443 true] [17592186672616 1083 